# Laramine

Early MIT Laravel core. Domain goal is Redmine 7.0.1 semantics, reimplemented in original PHP. Read `AGENTS.md` before a large change. The P0 layout, users and authentication, identity, projects nested-set, workflows, custom fields, queries, journals, time entries and attachments, outbound mail, activity, news, documents, and files, wiki, boards and forums, calendar and Gantt, Textile and Markdown rendering, wiki HTTP, boards and forums HTTP, and the notification and activity rows for those modules in `docs/parity-checklist.md` are **VERIFIED** by the tests named there. The full REST API row is **VERIFIED** by `tests/Parity/RestApiParityTest.php`. OpenID Connect is **N/A**. Activity for changesets stays **NOT VERIFIED**. Wiki and boards visual UX stays **NOT VERIFIED**. Every other row is **NOT VERIFIED**. Do not describe the project as production-ready.

## Architecture

- `app/Domain/Issues` — `IssueService` create/update, nested set, workflow, journal write (notes, private notes, attribute diffs, custom-value diffs, relation-add). `JournalNoteService` quotes, edits, and deletes a note under the same permissions as the history markers. History lines for `attr`, `attachment`, `relation`, and `cf` are compared on the journals row by `tests/Parity/JournalParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/Acl` — `PermissionCatalog`, `PermissionService`, `MembershipService`, `UserVisibility`. Permission names are catalog strings. `roles.permissions` is stored as a JSON array.
- `app/Domain/Workflow` — transitions (`WorkflowTransition`) and field rules (`WorkflowPermission`). MVP smoke: `docs/acl-workflow-parity-gate.md` (a checklist **PASS** there is Laramine smoke, not a 0.1 tag). The workflows checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/WorkflowParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/CustomFields` — formats and `CustomValueService`. Version values follow `versions.sharing`. See `docs/custom-fields.md`. The checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/CustomFieldParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/Queries` — `IssueQuery` runs and is the queries checklist comparison. `UserQuery` runs a limited catalog inside `UserVisibility` and is compared on the users and authentication row. `TimeEntryQuery` runs and is compared on the time entries row. `ProjectQuery` and `ProjectAdminQuery` run through `ProjectQueryRunner` and are compared by `tests/Parity/CalendarGanttQueryParityTest.php` and `tests/Parity/QueryRemainderParityTest.php`. See `docs/queries.md`.
- `app/Domain/Projects` — project nested set and modules.
- `app/Domain/News`, `app/Domain/Documents`, and `app/Domain/Files` — news, documents, and project files. The checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/ModulesNewsDocumentsFilesParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/Wiki` — pages, versions, redirects, protection, and watchers. The checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/WikiParityTest.php`. Rendered wiki HTML is the Textile and Markdown row.
- `app/Domain/TextFormatting` — `text_formatting` as textile, CommonMark, or plain, including Redmine links and core macros. The checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/MarkupParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/Boards` — nested boards, topics, replies, and watchers. The checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/BoardsParityTest.php`.
- `app/Domain/Notifications` — queued account, issue, news, document, file, message, and wiki mail. Account and issue mail are **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/NotificationParityTest.php`. News, document, and file mail, and message and wiki mail, are the separate rows in that test.
- `app/Domain/Activity` — issue, journal, time-entry, news, document, file, wiki, and message activity plus Atom feeds. Issues, journals, and time entries are **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/ActivityParityTest.php`. News, documents, and files, and wiki and messages, are the separate rows in that test. Changesets stay **NOT VERIFIED**.
- `app/Models` — Eloquent over Redmine 7.0.1 table and column names. Timestamp columns are `created_on` / `updated_on` where the schema says so. STI `type` values are Redmine class names.
- `app/Policies` — project, issue, news, and document abilities.
- `routes/web.php` — Inertia health smoke page at `GET /`, session sign-in and sign-out (`GET /login` is the Inertia sign-in page; `?view=blade` keeps the Blade form), account routes for registration, activation, lost password, password change, two-factor, preferences, the user directory, and account administration, `GET /users/current.json` and `GET /my.atom` as auth probes, activity and issue Atom feeds (`GET /activity`, `GET /activity.atom`, `GET /issues.atom`, and the same paths under `/projects/{identifier}/`), OAuth authorization-code token and revoke, authorized custom-field attachment download, attachment delete, and link URL resolution, container attachment upload, claim, download, thumbnail, download-all zip (`issues`, `journals`, `projects`, `versions`, `news`, `documents`, `wiki_pages`, `messages`), and delete, minimal news, document, and file pages, minimal calendar, gantt, and project-list pages, and functional wiki and board pages. Object type `files` is not on the zip route. There is no general HTTP API. The pages are not UI-ready and not a 0.1 tag (`docs/ux-parity-notes.md`). The custom fields checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/CustomFieldParityTest.php`. Container download and PNG thumbnails are compared on the time entries row. The activity checklist row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/ActivityParityTest.php`. The news, documents, and files row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/ModulesNewsDocumentsFilesParityTest.php`. The calendar and Gantt row is **VERIFIED** only by `tests/Parity/CalendarGanttQueryParityTest.php`.
- Users and authentication — founder lock in `docs/users-auth-spec.md` (2026-10-07). The session guard and the Redmine-shaped digest stay. Phase 2 adds registration, `must_change_passwd`, and `recovery` / `register` tokens. Phases 3–10 add LDAP (in-memory adapter), TOTP, OAuth authorization code as 7.0.1 core ships it, API and feed tokens, the user directory, account administration, preferences, and session / autologin tokens. Do not add a second auth stack, a bcrypt password column, Sanctum, Fortify, Jetstream, Passport, a live LDAP client, or OpenID Connect. The compared checklist rows are not a 0.1 tag. `users_visibility` is compared on the identity row.
- Schema pin: `docs/schema-inventory.md` and `docs/sources/redmine-7.0.1-schema.rb` (structure dump only).

Intentional differences belong in the matching doc. Do not silently “correct” them toward an unverified reading of Redmine.

## Quality bar

Locked. Do not weaken CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`).

- Pint: `composer lint` (`vendor/bin/pint --test`).
- Larastan / PHPStan level 8: `composer stan`. No baseline file. Do not add one without an explicit debt note in `QUALITY.md`.
- PHPUnit Unit + Feature + Parity on MySQL 8: `composer test`. Credentials are forced in `phpunit.xml` (`laramine_testing`, `root` / `password`, `127.0.0.1:3306`).
- Frontend scaffold: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` (Node 22). Do not drop that CI job. It does not verify UX parity.
- SQLite is a local migrate smoke only. Do not point PHPUnit or CI at it.
- No Pest config. PHP is `^8.2`; CI is PHP 8.3.

Green CI is required to merge.

## Clean-room

Redmine is GPLv2. Use behavior and schema semantics only. Never copy Ruby, ERB, JavaScript, upstream tests, or other GPLv2 source into the tree, commits, or generated files.

## Naming and style

- Domain services are `final` classes under `App\Domain\...`.
- Domain failures extend `App\Domain\DomainException` (`PermissionDeniedException`, `WorkflowDeniedException`, `CustomFieldValidationException`, `QueryValidationException`).
- Keep Redmine table, column, permission, and STI names. New JSON codecs go in existing text columns when the docs already say the column is JSON.
- Imports at the top of the file. Code comments in English. Exhaustive `match` on backed enums.
- Tests are `test_*` methods. Feature and most domain unit tests use `RefreshDatabase`. Reuse `Tests\Support\DomainFixture` when the scenario needs a project, tracker, statuses, and a member.

## Tests and docs

- Unit for formats, operators, and pure decisions. Feature for MySQL service behavior, including a deny path when permissions change. Parity only for a real Redmine 7.0.1 comparison.
- Do not set a parity row to VERIFIED from a passing Unit or Feature test.
- Behavior changes update `docs/domain.md`, `docs/custom-fields.md`, or `docs/queries.md` in the same change. Schema changes update `docs/schema-inventory.md`.
- Skip new markdown when behavior, setup, and the quality bar are unchanged.
- Continuing issues, queries, or custom fields: follow `.cursor/skills/continue-domain-work/SKILL.md`.

## Pull requests

State behavior changed, tests added or updated, and parity rows touched. Prefer a small diff. `CONTRIBUTING.md` is the human version of this rule.
